Expected elements: present

**On the ABI element (my P1 from r1): I consider Rule 2 satisfied and I am withdrawing it.** My finding asked for an action; the investigation showed the action cannot exist. Decisively, the element's action branch is conditioned on *raw bytes* — and this transaction has none (`Raw —`). An ABI decodes call data; there is no call data. So a `supply an ABI` control here would be inert even in a product that accepted ABIs, which makes it precisely the "retry that cannot succeed" §1 calls an honesty failure and this page's MUST-NOT-SHOW calls a disabled stand-in. Rule 2 admits "data, or a statement of why not"; the note gives both, and states that nothing would fix it. The expectation was not weakened to get there. Element present.

Register is right: light canvas, near-black geometric sans, mono texture on every hash, no Debug affordance, no empty panel. (b) reads as fixed — `BlockTracer` is the correct product-side noun.

Findings: the hero shows only green `Succeeded` while `Pending` finality sits at row six of Overview, so a glance reads settled. Section rules appear above Overview / Decoded input / Events / Raw but not above Internal calls or State changes. Absent data speaks two dialects — the AGE chip `No timestamp published` versus RAW's bare `—`. Plus copy and chip-tone nits.

Top fixes: lift the finality badge into the hero; give RAW the AGE row's labelled chip.

